 abstract = {Equilibration times for determining the leaf water potential (PSI(w)) of almond and lemon trees measured psychrometrically were obtained and found to be very long. The psychrometric dewpoint readings for leaves in a wide range of leaf water potential determined 5 minutes after the sample had been introduced into the psychrometer chamber were found to be linearly related to the values obtained when temperature and vapour pressure had reached steady state. This allowed the water potential to be obtained in a much shorter time than usual. The water potentials obtained by the proposed method showed a good correlation with xylem pressure potential (PSI(x) values obtained by a pressure chamber). Via S Michele Degli Scalzi, 2 Pisa 56100, Italy},
