 abstract = {A model has been developed to determine optimal irrigation strategies for a single season, Application of the model to a case study is presented and then analysed to illustrate the use of the technique and to develop some general guidelines. The multiple results prove that the normal strategy of adopting a single value to the 'gross water depth applied/water depth needed' which depends on the irrigation system is not acceptable. This is because agronomic and economic factors should also be taken into account, plus the volume of available water on the farm and the price per cubic metre of water placed in the field.},
